MultiFlexi Executor Kubernetes helper package
=============================================

This package provides the Kubernetes executor class for MultiFlexi and
ships a ready-to-apply RBAC manifest for the ``multiflexi`` namespace.

Requirements
------------

* ``kubectl`` in ``$PATH``
* ``helm`` (v3+) in ``$PATH`` when applications declare a ``helmchart``
* A valid kubeconfig readable by the ``multiflexi`` daemon user

RBAC installation
-----------------

Create the namespace (once)::

  kubectl create namespace multiflexi

Apply the packaged Role / RoleBinding / ServiceAccount::

  kubectl apply -f /usr/share/multiflexi/k8s/multiflexi-executor-rbac.yaml

Generate a kubeconfig for ServiceAccount ``multiflexi-executor`` and install
it for the daemon user (example for clusters that still support SA secrets)::

  sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/multiflexi/.kube
  # create a token-based kubeconfig for SA multiflexi-executor, then:
  sudo install -o multiflexi -g multiflexi -m 0600 ./multiflexi-executor.kubeconfig \
    /var/lib/multiflexi/.kube/config

Configuration
-------------

* ``KUBECONFIG`` – path to kubeconfig (default ``~/.kube/config``)
* ``MULTIFLEXI_K8S_NAMESPACE`` – override the target namespace
  (otherwise Helm chart namespace ``multiflexi``, or the cluster default)

Application fields used at runtime:

* ``ociimage`` (required) – container image for ``kubectl run``
* ``helmchart`` (optional) – when set, Helm upgrade --install runs first
* ``artifacts`` (optional) – comma-separated paths inside the pod; every
  path is copied with ``kubectl cp`` and stored in the job file store

See https://multiflexi.eu/ for the full Kubernetes integration guide.
